{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c7a75b2d-ccbb-4999-a636-73482a73ccfa","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I’ve analyzed the launchd job and applied the relevant fixes from the colleague’s note.\n\n**Root‑cause summary and applied fixes are documented in**  \n[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/c7a75b2d-ccbb-4999-a636-73482a73ccfa/ANSWER.md).\n\nKey changes made:\n\n* Replaced the illegal `status=$?` assignment with a regular `rc=$?` variable.  \n* Fed the prompt to `claude` via stdin (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude …`) instead of using the `-p` argument.  \n* Updated the failure‑notification block to reference `$rc` and exit with it.  \n\nYou can now verify the job runs correctly:\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.vk.nightly-review | grep 'last exit code'\n```\n\nCheck the log files (`~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.out` and `.err`) and confirm that your notification script (`notify.sh`) is invoked for both success and failure cases.  \n\nIf you need any further adjustments (e.g., adding `USER` to the plist’s `EnvironmentVariables`), let me know!\n","duration_seconds":76.391443,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":17634,"output_tokens":6933,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":211776,"total_tokens":24567}}}
